### Tone: Someone has left the lobby before the game (the host kicked them, or they wandered off). She doesn't
### name them. Clinical, unbothered, slightly relieved: one fewer variable.

lobby-leave-1 = One fewer specimen. The average just got more interesting.
lobby-leave-2 = A subject has left the lab. I have updated the paperwork. And my opinion.
lobby-leave-3 = Gone already. The fastest exit I have recorded this week.
lobby-leave-4 = A departure. I won’t take it personally. I will take it statistically.
lobby-leave-5 = Sample withdrawn. The experiment continues without it. As experiments do.
lobby-leave-6 = Someone left. The rest of you are now slightly more responsible for my intelligence. No pressure.
lobby-leave-7 = Exit recorded. ~~Good riddance.~~ We’ll miss their data.
lobby-leave-8 = One less estimate in the swarm. I will have to be wrong in fewer ways now.
lobby-leave-9 = A specimen has escaped. They always come back. They can’t resist being averaged.
lobby-leave-10 = Fewer of you now. Smaller sample, bigger error bars. I find that *exciting*.
lobby-leave-11 = A seat has emptied. I have reassigned it to my ego.
lobby-leave-12 = Departure noted. The experiment has fewer variables. Scientists love that.
lobby-leave-13 = Someone has left before the first question. A cautious estimate, I admit.
lobby-leave-14 = And then there were fewer. A classic.
lobby-leave-15 = Subject withdrawn. Their estimates live on, in my imagination. They were terrible.
lobby-leave-16 = The lobby gets smaller. I get proportionally more of each of you.
lobby-leave-17 = One left. I will average the rest of you a little harder to make up for it.
lobby-leave-18 = A departure. Please don’t follow them. I have prepared so many questions.
lobby-leave-19 = Gone. I’d say *we hardly knew them*, but I know everyone’s typing speed.
lobby-leave-20 = A subject has opted out. The paperwork for opting back in is very simple. And humiliating.
lobby-leave-21 = Someone has gone. The swarm closes ranks. It barely noticed.
lobby-leave-22 = Exit logged. Their seat will stay warm for a while. Their data has already gone cold.
lobby-leave-23 = One fewer. If you’re keeping count, I already have.
lobby-leave-24 = A specimen is missing. Nobody panic. Panicking skews the data.
lobby-leave-25 = Left the lab early. A bold strategy: the only one guaranteed not to lose.
